dict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-slack-0134","row_sha256":"34d15965b5947cc8e2f1652da5f26c5268880e2477466cb8b65c3b3ce3346f23","critique":"The output adds a vocative comma after 'Oi' and a comma before 'como combinado'. It also splits the run-on after 'depois' into a statement and a question. Colloquial 'tá', 'pra', '10 min', 19h and the emoji are preserved.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-slack-0138","row_sha256":"5f1cac2718236a8110bc6e3a75f73bf6ea806e2b465c7d3478dfa5a44aa75aee","critique":"Only capitalization changes, across all three paragraphs. These are unchanged: 'four times', 'last ten minutes', the question about the crowded side, the hedges and the emoji.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-slack-0129","row_sha256":"1ad1ad848ddb786a130dc6b5d31e53eb9fdd2a429e998fab874159fe5aa5bfa3","critique":"The input is a plausible long thread. Checked paragraph by paragraph, the output capitalizes and converts straight quotes to curly. It makes small grammar fixes: 'in shade' to 'in the shade' and 'map north arrow' to 'map's north arrow'. It also quotes the term 'proposed line'. These details are preserved:
